# Mobile (React Native) boundaries

- This is **React Native + Expo** (prebuild / dev client). Do **not** use `next/*`, server components,
  SSR, Playwright, or `@podverse/ui` (components/SCSS).
- **Themes:** import `@podverse/design-tokens` and use **mobile-theme-parity** skill — same theme IDs
  and token values as web; RN `ThemeProvider` + `StyleSheet`, not CSS.
- **Visual parity:** when a screen has a web counterpart, reference the web design first
  (`apps/web/src/app/<area>/` route client + `apps/web/src/components/<Area>/`) and mirror its
  layout / information hierarchy / list-row structure / loading-empty-error states, adapted to RN
  primitives with design tokens (no hardcoded hex). See **mobile-theme-parity** § Screen & visual
  parity. Diverge only for platform conventions and note why.
- Mobile is a **Tier 5 consumer** — import downward only. See
  [apps/mobile/AGENTS.md](/apps/mobile/AGENTS.md) allowlist/denylist and
  [architecture-tier-dependencies](/.cursor/rules/architecture-tier-dependencies.mdc).
- Do **not** import server/web-only packages: `@podverse/orm`, `@podverse/parser`, `@podverse/mq`,
  `@podverse/helpers-backend`, `@podverse/helpers-browser`, `@podverse/helpers-config`,
  `@podverse/observability`, `@podverse/external-services-*`.
- **Auth:** bearer + secure storage; never cookies / `withCredentials`. See
  [API-CLIENT-BOUNDARIES.md](/docs/development/API-CLIENT-BOUNDARIES.md) and `/auth/mobile/*`.
- **Env config:** prefer env vars over hardcoded values when practical. All
  `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` reads live under `apps/mobile/src/config/` (`env.ts` literals;
  `getMobileConfig()` is the consumer-facing entry). Outside `src/config/`, do **not**
  read `process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_*` — use `getMobileConfig()` instead. Mobile API wiring
  uses `EXPO_PUBLIC_MOBILE_API_BASE_URL[_IOS|_ANDROID]` (must include `/api/<version>` in
  the URL); invalid or pathless URLs fail validation (no call-site / factory path fallbacks).
- Reuse `@podverse/helpers-requests` via **`ApiRequestService` instance methods**
  (e.g. `createMobileApiRequestService()?.reqAuthMobileToken(...)`). Standalone `req*` helpers in
  package source are not all re-exported from the barrel — prefer methods on the service instance.
  Also reuse `@podverse/playback-core` policy; implement transport via a **native bridge**
  (`NativePlaybackBridge`) — do not edit web `useMediaElementBridge` for mobile.
- **ApiRequestService contract:** base URL is composed as `${prefix.replace(/\/$/, '')}${version}`.
  Keep `prefix` with no trailing slash and `version` with a leading slash (`/api` + `/v2`).
  Those fields come from `getMobileConfig().api` (parsed from the base URL env).
- **`@podverse/helpers`:** do not import the package barrel on mobile — it re-exports Node-only modules
  (`crypto`, etc.). Use documented subpath exports (e.g. `@podverse/helpers/locales`) or add new subpaths;
  see [APPS-MOBILE.md § Troubleshooting](/apps/mobile/APPS-MOBILE.md) (Node stdlib bundling).
- **Expo env access:** Expo inlines only literal `process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_*` references. Never use
  dynamic `process.env[...]` or destructuring for mobile env vars. Keep those literals in
  `apps/mobile/src/config/env.ts` only.
- **Validation reuse:** `@podverse/helpers-config` is backend/web focused and validates by dynamic
  `process.env[varName]`, which is not mobile-safe. For shared validation logic, use value-based
  helpers from `@podverse/helpers` plus a mobile-local wrapper (`validateMobileEnv.ts`).
- **Import specifiers (Tier D):** extensionless relative imports in app source. See
  [DOCS-DEVELOPMENT-TOOLING-IMPORT-SPECIFIERS.md § Tier D](/docs/development/tooling/DOCS-DEVELOPMENT-TOOLING-IMPORT-SPECIFIERS.md).
- **Generic helpers:** if a function is not specifically tied to one screen/component (HTTP error
  parsing, pure formatting, assertion-free error shape reads, etc.), put it in
  `apps/mobile/src/lib/` (or the nearest domain module under `src/auth|config|i18n|…` when that
  domain owns it) **when first written**, even with a single callsite. Do not wait for a second
  consumer. Prefer mobile-local `src/lib/` over a new package when the helper depends on
  mobile/request error shapes or RN-only concerns.
- **Reusable first (DRY):** prioritize generic reusable components, hooks, and pure functions early.
  If two screens share the same UI/state pattern (screen scaffold + loading/error/auth-empty states,
  section cards, row mappers, queue/history loaders, add-by-rss async flow, etc.), extract into
  `apps/mobile/src/components/`, `apps/mobile/src/hooks/`, or `apps/mobile/src/lib/` instead of
  duplicating logic in screen files. Prefer small composable primitives over large screen-specific
  implementations, and keep feature behavior wired through shared abstractions whenever possible.
- **Async naming (`fetch` vs `load`/`reload`):** split verbs by responsibility so names never collide
  when a screen orchestrator wraps a resource hook:
  - `fetch<Resource>` — pure data fetch (returns DTOs/rows; **no** `setState` / loading/error ownership).
    Use in resource hooks and pure helpers (e.g. `fetchPrimaryQueue`, `fetchHistoryPage`,
    `fetchHomeFeedRows`).
  - `load<Resource>` — stateful orchestrator that sets `isLoading` / `errorKey` / local data (and may
    call one or more `fetch*` helpers). Prefer this name on screens and content-load hooks.
  - `reload<Resource>` / `refresh<Resource>` — re-run a loader (retry, pull-to-refresh, after mutate).
  Do **not** expose a hook method named `loadX` when screens will also declare a local `loadX`
  wrapper — that causes `Identifier already been declared` Metro failures. Prefer distinct verbs
  over destructuring aliases (`loadHistory: loadHistoryResources`).
- **E2E:** Maestro in `apps/mobile/e2e/` — **not** `make e2e_*` (web/management-web only).
  After mobile UI/feature work, end responses with the focused `npm run mobile:e2e:test -- <area>`
  + slot report paths (**mobile-e2e-screenshots**, **end-with-targeted-make-report-verify**).
- **Playback parity:** [DOCS-MOBILE-PROCESS-PLAYBACK-QUEUE-PARITY.md](/docs/proposals/mobile/app-development-process/DOCS-MOBILE-PROCESS-PLAYBACK-QUEUE-PARITY.md).
